
title: Anni di piombo
new-page: true

on-arrival: {! if (typeof Q.inflation !== 'number') Q.inflation = 65; if (typeof Q.public_support !== 'number') Q.public_support = 50; if (typeof Q.security !== 'number') Q.security = 45; if (typeof Q.stability !== 'number') Q.stability = 55; if (typeof Q.month !== 'number') Q.month = 12; if (typeof Q.year !== 'number') Q.year = 1969; if (typeof Q.party_name !== 'string') Q.party_name = 'Not selected'; !}

ITALY, DECEMBER 1969

The Italian Republic is entering a period of profound political crisis. Bombings, street clashes, militant organisations and industrial unrest are testing the institutions of the post-war state.

You will lead a political party through the Years of Lead. Every policy has consequences. Economic pressure, public support, public security and political stability will shape your future.

Choose your political organisation.

- @dc_start: Democrazia Cristiana (DC)
- @pci_start: Partito Comunista Italiano (PCI)
- @psi_start: Partito Socialista Italiano (PSI)
- @msi_start: Movimento Sociale Italiano (MSI)


@dc_start
title: Christian Democracy
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.party_name = 'DC'; Q.public_support = 52; Q.stability = 58; !}

**Democrazia Cristiana**

The Christian Democrats dominate the governing system but face pressure from labour unrest, the communist opposition and internal divisions.

Your challenge is to preserve parliamentary government while responding to social demands and political violence.

- @piazza_fontana: Continue to the national crisis


@pci_start
title: Italian Communist Party
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.party_name = 'PCI'; Q.public_support = 48; Q.stability = 48; !}

**Partito Comunista Italiano**

The Communist Party has a powerful working-class base and substantial electoral support, but remains excluded from national government by Cold War alignments.

Your challenge is to turn social mobilisation into political influence without deepening the crisis.

- @piazza_fontana: Continue to the national crisis


@psi_start
title: Italian Socialist Party
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.party_name = 'PSI'; Q.public_support = 42; Q.stability = 50; !}

**Partito Socialista Italiano**

The Socialists occupy a difficult position between reformist government and pressure from the labour movement.

Your challenge is to pursue reforms while holding together a divided political coalition.

- @piazza_fontana: Continue to the national crisis


@msi_start
title: Italian Social Movement
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.party_name = 'MSI'; Q.public_support = 28; Q.stability = 38; !}

**Movimento Sociale Italiano**

The post-fascist right seeks a larger role in national politics amid street violence, polarisation and growing distrust of the political establishment.

Your challenge is to expand your influence in a fragile parliamentary system.

- @piazza_fontana: Continue to the national crisis


@piazza_fontana
title: Piazza Fontana
subtitle: Milan — 12 December 1969
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.security = Math.max(0, Q.security - 8); Q.stability = Math.max(0, Q.stability - 7); !}

**A bombing shakes the Republic**

On 12 December 1969, a bomb exploded at the Piazza Fontana bank in Milan, killing 17 people and injuring many others. The attack became a defining event in Italy's Years of Lead.

The country demands answers. Rumours spread, political tensions intensify and the authorities face pressure to act.

How will your political leadership respond?

- @public_inquiry: Demand a transparent investigation
- @security_response: Prioritise emergency security measures
- @calm_appeal: Appeal for restraint and national unity


@public_inquiry
title: Demand an Investigation
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.public_support = Math.min(100, Q.public_support + 5); Q.stability = Math.min(100, Q.stability + 2); Q.security = Math.min(100, Q.security + 1); !}

You call for a thorough investigation, public accountability and respect for constitutional safeguards.

The appeal reassures citizens who fear abuses of power, though some political opponents accuse you of weakening the authorities.

- @monthly_briefing: Enter government


@security_response
title: Emergency Security Measures
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.security = Math.min(100, Q.security + 8); Q.public_support = Math.max(0, Q.public_support - 3); Q.stability = Math.max(0, Q.stability - 2); !}

You support stronger security measures and demand rapid action from the authorities.

Some citizens welcome a firm response. Others fear that emergency measures could undermine civil liberties and increase political polarisation.

- @monthly_briefing: Enter government


@calm_appeal
title: National Unity Appeal
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.public_support = Math.min(100, Q.public_support + 3); Q.stability = Math.min(100, Q.stability + 4); !}

You appeal for restraint, reject political violence and call for cooperation across democratic institutions.

The speech offers a brief moment of calm, but citizens expect practical action.

- @monthly_briefing: Enter government



@monthly_briefing
title: Government
subtitle: Italy — [+ month +] / [+ year +]
new-page: true
is-hand: true
max-cards: 3

**THE GOVERNMENT**

Your party: [+ party_name +]

The country faces economic pressure and political violence. Draw policy cards from the deck and choose which measures to pursue.

Each card represents a government initiative. Its consequences will affect the balance of power and the stability of the Republic.

- @policy_deck
- #pinnedCard


@policy_deck
title: Government Policy Deck
subtitle: Draw a policy card
is-deck: true

- #policy_deck


@economic_relief
title: Economic Relief
subtitle: Wages, prices and living standards
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: policy_deck

Prices and wages are under pressure. Your government proposes targeted relief and negotiations with trade unions.

- @relief_success: Fund the relief programme
- @return_government: Return without action


@relief_success
title: Relief Programme Approved
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.inflation = Math.max(0, Q.inflation - 5); Q.public_support = Math.min(100, Q.public_support + 4); Q.stability = Math.max(0, Q.stability - 1); !}

The government commits to economic relief. Workers welcome the measure, but business leaders question its cost.

- @monthly_briefing: Return to government


@public_security
title: Public Security
subtitle: Policing and civil liberties
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: policy_deck

Political violence is putting pressure on the government to act. You must balance public safety with democratic safeguards.

- @security_success: Expand security operations
- @return_government: Return without action


@security_success
title: Security Measures Approved
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.security = Math.min(100, Q.security + 6); Q.public_support = Math.max(0, Q.public_support - 2); Q.stability = Math.min(100, Q.stability + 1); !}

The government expands security operations. Some citizens feel safer, while civil-liberties advocates demand oversight.

- @monthly_briefing: Return to government


@institutional_reform
title: Institutional Reform
subtitle: Parliament and democratic legitimacy
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: policy_deck

Your government proposes reforms intended to rebuild public confidence and strengthen democratic institutions.

- @reform_success: Begin reform negotiations
- @return_government: Return without action


@reform_success
title: Reform Negotiations
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.public_support = Math.min(100, Q.public_support + 3); Q.stability = Math.min(100, Q.stability + 4); !}

Negotiations begin. Reform could strengthen democratic legitimacy, but entrenched political interests may resist.

- @monthly_briefing: Return to government


@return_government
title: Return to Government
go-to: monthly_briefing


@advance_month
title: A New Month
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.month = Q.month + 1; if (Q.month > 12) { Q.month = 1; Q.year = Q.year + 1; } Q.inflation = Math.min(100, Q.inflation + 2); Q.stability = Math.max(0, Q.stability - 1); !}

**The calendar moves forward**

Another month begins. Economic pressure continues, political factions manoeuvre and the government must decide what to prioritise next.

Your administration remains under pressure to deliver results.

- @monthly_briefing: Continue governing
